  "Authority": "Operator verdict log for the taped light mounts, which are on by default (wave 16 owner decision: enable all features by default). Every authored pair is admitted unverified at startup unless EnableTapedPackMounts is off or its row here has Disabled=true; absent or false Disabled means admitted. Checked, CheckDate and Note are the operator's own record of a client check (Checked=true needs a CheckDate and a Note) and change nothing else. The admission log line says admitted unverified: no native or two-client verdict is recorded and nothing here is DayZ evidence (runtime=PENDING). An unknown PairId, a duplicate, a non-bool Checked or Disabled, or a malformed file refuses the whole file and the module reports degraded with the reason. Wave 15: one row per approved cross-slot weapon pair (TLRLight on the rail rifles, UniversalLight on the pistols); the ids are derived from the HCTapedLightCatalog rows by HCTapedLightCatalog.CrossPairIds and unit tests pin that this file lists exactly those ids. A pair still needs its native slot arrays: a missing slot is logged once as a named refusal, never a silent skip.",
